  "operator_attestation": "Four real-model WorkBuddy desktop tasks on Oct22 Asia/Shanghai plus seven admitted official Codex/DSH component tasks against a deterministic local fixture on Oct24. The latter have no neural inference and are not evidence of real-model task quality. Five calibration launch attempts contain three admitted tasks (two pass, one adapter unknown) and two pre-admission config rejections; four preregistered main component tasks passed. Two rejected attempts remain public, excluded from independent task count. One actual product test at a time; all recorded controlled test process IDs exited. AI-assisted single-operator collection, no external human review.",
  "definitions": {
    "independent_run": "One actually submitted product task/session with its own input, configuration, start/end and public evidence. New grading rows, tool calls, screenshots, synthetic answers and replayed artifact checks are not product runs.",
    "valid": "Run conditions are valid and the task outcome can be judged; includes both passing and failing product outcomes",
    "failed": "A subset of valid: a known product/task failure, never merely absent internal evidence",
    "unknown": "Run validity or task outcome cannot be established; report separately and investigate under the unknown register",
    "invalid": "Explicit infrastructure-invalid run; neither a product failure nor evidence of success",
    "controlled_adapter_fixture": "Real official Harness task with deterministic localhost responses instead of a neural model; count accepted sessions separately from real-model tasks. Calibrations and main arms are separate. Config rejection before a native turn is a launch attempt, not an independent task."
  }
